<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giuseppe Garibaldi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1807–1882</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Garibaldi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giuseppe Garibaldi was an Italian revolutionary and soldier, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a>. In exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> he fought for the Riograndense Republic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a>. He defended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> in 1849 and in 1860 led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/expedition-of-the-thousand">Expedition of the Thousand</a> that conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, a decisive step in the unification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi.jpg" alt="Giuseppe Garibaldi" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Salvatore Lo Forte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Giuseppe_Garibaldi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
